assets.prompt:
Create a high-resolution photorealistic MATERIAL AND CONSTRUCTION DETAIL SHEET for the exact same mass-timber biophilic hospital in the supplied references. Use a clean 3-by-2 grid of six equal rectangular close-up panels with thin neutral separators and no captions, typography or labels. Every panel must be square-on, evenly illuminated, perspective-correct and suitable as a source for physically based material textures:

1) honey-toned vertical timber rainscreen and closely spaced solar-control fins, fine straight grain, narrow dark joints, subtle board variation, concealed fasteners and matte exterior oil;
2) exposed glulam column/beam/CLT slab-edge junction, laminated layers and end grain visible, crisp joinery plate/bolt detail, warm matte clearcoat, no decorative carving;
3) shou-sugi-ban charred-black vertical timber public/service plinth, restrained alligator grain, charcoal variation, deep joints and durable base flashing;
4) low pale board-formed concrete/local stone plinth and calm grey forecourt paving, fine mineral aggregate, crisp arris, expansion joint and minor realistic staining;
5) living-wall and integrated planter construction, modular green-wall backing, irrigation line, ferns/vines, a timber or dark-metal edge, meadow grasses and believable soil depth without jungle density;
6) rooftop assembly: dark photovoltaic module with realistic cells/frame, black louvered mechanical screen, dark parapet flashing, gravel fire break and sedum roof edge with roof build-up depth.

Match the colour temperature, materials and construction quality of the supplied hospital exactly. Architectural product photography, sharp microdetail, shadow-neutral soft daylight, physically plausible roughness. No cartoon, collage embellishment, hands, tools, text, logos, watermarks, extra materials, windows printed into timber or dramatic directional shadows.
